+</div>
+<h1>Informer Long Sequence</h1>
+<p class="lede">A long-horizon transformer forecaster for farm power, built on sparse attention that scales linearly instead of quadratically in sequence length. Its forecast residual is an anomaly signal, and its horizon is what makes day-ahead planning possible at all.</p>
+<div class="cta">
+<a class="btn" href="https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-informer-long-sequence">View on GitHub</a>
+<a class="btn ghost" href="https://rajaram-2005.github.io/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/ecosystem.html">25-model ecosystem graph</a>
+<a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/rajaram-2005/wt-pm-lstm-scada-anomaly/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md">Platform architecture</a>
+</div>
+</header>
+<p class="note">This page is generated from <code>deployment/models.catalog.json</code> in the reference repository, together with the other 24 model pages, so all 25 agree on numbering, contract and status.</p>
+<h2>Model</h2>
+<ul>
+<li><code>Informer model in model.py</code></li>
+<li><code>ProbSparse attention block</code> - self-declared placeholder upstream</li>
+</ul>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Encoder</th><td>ProbSparse self-attention plus a distilling step that halves sequence length per layer</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Decoder</th><td>Generative-style decoder producing the whole forecast horizon in one forward pass</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Output</th><td>Multi-step power forecast; residual against actuals becomes the anomaly score</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h2>Advanced concepts</h2>
+<p class="note">The ideas this model actually leans on, each stated with its failure mode.</p>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Sparse attention</h3>
+<p>Only the queries with the most 'active' attention distributions are evaluated, reducing cost from O(L^2) to O(L log L). That is the entire reason a long-horizon transformer is deployable on 10-minute SCADA at all.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Distilling layers</h3>
+<p>Each encoder layer halves the sequence, so depth buys global context instead of memory. The trade is resolution: fine structure must be captured early or it is gone.</p>
+</div>
+<div class="card">
+<h3>Partial - and labelled that way</h3>
+<p>Upstream ships a placeholder attention implementation. The adapter runs the real graph but the attention is not the published ProbSparse kernel, so the forecast error is honest but the architecture claim is not. Marking it partial is the point.</p>
+</div>
+<h2>Platform contract</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Input (adapter view)</th><td>long windows</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Output</th><td>prediction (power forecast) + anomaly_score (forecast residual)</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Record format</th><td><code>wt-pm.platform.v1</code></td></tr>
+<tr><th>Typical latency</th><td>8000 ms</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Deployment targets</th><td>cloud</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Requirements</th><td>torch</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Fallback</th><td>m03-tcn-power-curve</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Subsystem focus</th><td>whole turbine</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Hermes tool</th><td><code>anomaly / planning context</code></td></tr>
+</table>
+<p class="note">Records follow the shared <code>WTDataSchema</code> (<code>wt-pm.platform.v1</code>). Only <code>timestamp</code>, <code>turbine_id</code> and <code>model_id</code> are required; absence is distinguishable from a zero.</p>
+<h2>Platform layers</h2>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Fusion</th><td>Forecast-residual anomaly voter and the long-horizon source for power-curve tracking</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Hermes</th><td>anomaly tool plus planning context for what_if</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Fallback</th><td>Falls back to m03-tcn-power-curve when torch is unavailable</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Evaluation</th><td>Scored on both forecast error and residual-based detection - a good forecaster can be a poor detector</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h2>How it connects to the other 24</h2>
+<ul class="edges">
+<li>&rarr; <b>21. TCN Power Curve</b> <span class="note">(m03-tcn-power-curve)</span> - long-horizon power forecast vs the actual curve</li>
+</ul>
+<h2>Honest limits</h2><ul class="limits">
+<li>Partial: attention is a placeholder, so results are not the published Informer</li>
+<li>8 s latency - cloud only</li>
+</ul>
+<p class="note">Fidelity: rung 1 of the fidelity ladder - simulator data, surrogate waveforms where stated, proxy RUL targets, simulator fault labels. Comparable within this collection, not field-validated turbine control.</p>
